note top of BaseController
  Base class for all controllers:
  • Standardized response methods
  • Error handling patterns
  • Request validation helpers
  • User ID extraction
end note

note top of BaseService
  Generic base class for services:
  • CRUD operations (findAll, findById, create, update, delete)
  • User isolation (userId filtering)
  • Data validation
  • Logger integration
  • Used by AIService, EmailService, PDFService
end note

note top of AgentOrchestrator
  Central orchestration service that:
  • Interprets user natural language (with language detection)
  • Determines appropriate tool/action
  • Executes actions via specialized services
  • Provides unified interface for AI agent
  • Default scheduling for cron jobs (0 9 * * *)
end note

note top of AIService
  AI Integration service:
  • Gemini AI API communication
  • User context management (via UserContextService)
  • Template generation
  • Multi-turn conversation
  • Language-aware responses (Polish/English)
end note

note top of UserContextService
  User context aggregation:
  • Recent emails summary
  • Active tasks overview
  • Notifications status
  • User settings
  • Formatted for AI context window
end note

note top of Logger
  Structured logging singleton:
  • Log levels: DEBUG, INFO, WARN, ERROR
  • Metadata support for structured logs
  • Correlation ID tracking
  • Used by all services and middleware
end note

note top of Cache
  In-memory LRU cache:
  • TTL-based expiration
  • Automatic eviction
  • Max size enforcement
  • Used for dashboard stats, user context
end note

note top of Config
  Centralized configuration:
  • Singleton pattern
  • Type-safe config access
  • Environment variable validation
  • Organized by domain (server, DB, AI, email, security, performance)
end note

note top of ErrorHandler
  Global error handling:
  • Catches all errors
  • asyncHandler wrapper for async routes
  • Operational vs programming errors
  • Structured error responses
end note

legend right
    **Architecture Patterns (Senior-Level Design)**
    |= Symbol / Kolor |= Znaczenie |
    | <back:#CE93D8>Controller</back> | Controllers (extend BaseController for standardized responses) |
    | <back:#81C784>BaseService</back> | Abstract base service with generic CRUD operations |
    | <back:#FFFDE7>Service</back> | Business logic services (extend BaseService) |
    | <back:#E3F2FD>Type</back> | Type definitions and data structures |
    | <back:#F3E5F5>Utility</back> | Utility classes (Logger, Cache, Performance, Encryption) |
    | <back:#FFF9C4>Middleware</back> | Express middleware (Auth, Logging, Rate Limiting, Validation) |
    | <back:#EF5350>Error</back> | Custom error classes (extend AppError) |
    | <back:#80CBC4>Singleton</back> | Singleton classes (Config, Logger, Cache) |
    | <back:#E8F5E9>Database</back> | Database access layer (Supabase) |
    | <back:#FFF3E0>Cloud</back> | Supabase cloud services |
    
    **Relationships:**
    | *-- | Composition (contains, manages lifecycle) |
    | o-- | Aggregation (has reference, doesn't manage lifecycle) |
    | --> | Usage or dependency |
    | --|> | Inheritance (extends/implements) |
    | ..> | Throws or instantiates |
    | <color:#1976D2>Blue</color> | Association relationships |
    | <color:#616161>Gray</color> | Inheritance relationships |
    | <color:#8E24AA>Purple</color> | Dependency relationships |
    
    **Key Improvements (Phase 2 Optimizations):**
    • **Controller Layer** - BaseController with standardized response methods
    • **BaseService<T>** - Generic base class with CRUD operations
    • **Structured Logging** - Logger singleton with correlation IDs
    • **In-Memory Caching** - LRU cache with TTL expiration
    • **Centralized Config** - Type-safe configuration management
    • **Error Hierarchy** - Custom errors (Validation, Auth, NotFound, Database)
    • **Rate Limiting** - Global + per-route rate limiting
    • **Request Tracing** - Correlation IDs for distributed tracing
    • **Performance Monitoring** - Performance utilities for metrics
    • **Language Detection** - Polish/English automatic detection
    • **User Context** - UserContextService for AI context aggregation
    • **Default Scheduling** - Automatic cron defaults (0 9 * * *)
    
    **Design Patterns:**
    • Singleton (Config, Logger, Cache)
    • Base Class Pattern (BaseController, BaseService)
    • Dependency Injection (services receive dependencies)
    • Repository Pattern (BaseService provides data access abstraction)
    • Middleware Chain (RequestLogger → RateLimiter → Auth → Validation)
    • Factory Pattern (error classes, middleware configurators)
endlegend

